  "title": "Marco Polo's journey to China",
  "summary": "In 1271 Marco Polo, aged 17, left Venice with his father Niccolo and uncle Maffeo for the court of Kublai Khan, going first by sea to Acre. After about three and a half years of travel they were welcomed at Shangdu, the khan's summer capital, in spring 1275. They left China in 1292 and reached Venice in 1295, twenty-four years after setting out.",
